{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971311-forcing-doors-and-hard-leverage","id":971311,"title":"Forcing doors and Hard Leverage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T07:35:52-07:00","id":971311,"title":"Forcing doors and Hard Leverage","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> one of the most things I really appreciate in VtR 2ed is the social maneuvering system but I'm wondering about a particular aspect of the rules: Hard Leverage.<br /> To define how many doors should be removed the GM assign a breaking point level to the action and the difference with humanity determines the doors removed.<br /> My point is: why a gun pointed by a low humanity/integrity vamp/man (maybe a soldier used to threathen) should be less effective then one handled by Saint Francis??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:49:08-07:00","id":971338,"title":"","content":"I see this with this mindframe &quot; The Character do a very bad action for his/hernormal behaviour, this is a risk for his/her Integrity/other trait: make this more worth giving a bonus.&quot;<br /> I am not totally fine because also the other line make very clear the idea &quot; I am a VERY hurt/bad/though/whatever people: my menace is more intimiditing because of this.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:20:43-07:00","id":971354,"title":"","content":"I think this is a result of translating the Hard Leverage rules across different Integrity systems. In vanilla, you remove one Door of the Breaking Point was -1 or -2, or two Doors if the Breaking Point was -3 or worse. In werewolf, Hard Leverage is always a Breaking Point towards Flesh; it removes two doors if the subject is a spirit and the actor's Harmony is 2 or less, or if the subject is a human and the actor's Harmony is 8 or more, otherwise it removes one Door. Mage references Humanity in the advance PDF, so hopefully it'll be changed in the final version, and Promethean doesn't actually mention Forcing Doors in the Social Maneuvering section. Not sure on Beast, as I don't have the book.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think tying Forcing Doors to Breaking Points was not the best decision, since different templates handle Breaking Points differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:29:43-07:00","id":971356,"title":"","content":"It shouldn't work with the difference between humanity and breaking point; it just should work with the &quot;level&quot; of the breaking point. A gun pointed to the head of someone is far more effective than a words threat (maybe with a roll on manipulation/strenght + intimidation/subterfuge - composure to see if the threat sounds credible).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:43:46-07:00","id":971397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971311-forcing-doors-and-hard-leverage?p=971356#post971356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It shouldn't work with the difference between humanity and breaking point; it just should work with the &quot;level&quot; of the breaking point. A gun pointed to the head of someone is far more effective than a words threat (maybe with a roll on manipulation/strenght + intimidation/subterfuge - composure to see if the threat sounds credible).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure if you're just verbally threatening them but don't have something to back it up - a weapon, blackmail material, etc. then that's not really Hard Leverage, that's just Forcing Doors. The term &quot;Leverage&quot; implies that you have something to actually leverage the subject with.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree, it would make more sense to be based on the Humanity level of the Breaking Point, not relative to the actor's Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:05:51-07:00","id":971413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971311-forcing-doors-and-hard-leverage?p=971397#post971397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure if you're just verbally threatening them but don't have something to back it up - a weapon, blackmail material, etc. then that's not really Hard Leverage, that's just Forcing Doors. The term &quot;Leverage&quot; implies that you have something to actually leverage the subject with.<br /> <br /> That said, I agree, it would make more sense to be based on the Humanity level of the Breaking Point, not relative to the actor's Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably I'm wrong but reading this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When forcing Doors, state your character\u2019s goal and her approach, then roll immediately </div> </div> </div>I think about some kind of insistence in the act of convince someone to give you / do that &quot;things&quot;. You want it and you want it now, but it doesen't imply to ask in a bad manner. You could even seduce him.<br /> <br /> And about hard leverage:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hard Leverage represents threats, drugging, intimidation, blackmail, kidnapping, or other heavy-handed forms of coercion. </div> </div> </div>it states about intimidation. Intimidation could be either without weapon (I'll kill your mother) or with weapon (bags or life). Could be weapon just a bonus dice maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:49:43-07:00","id":971432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971311-forcing-doors-and-hard-leverage?p=971413#post971413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably I'm wrong but reading this:<br /> <br /> I think about some kind of insistence in the act of convince someone to give you / do that &quot;things&quot;. You want it and you want it now, but it doesen't imply to ask in a bad manner. You could even seduce him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. Forcing Doors can be seduction, high-pressure sales tactics, coercion - anything where you're pressuring the subject into making a decision <i>right now</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971311-forcing-doors-and-hard-leverage?p=971413#post971413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And about hard leverage:<br /> <br /> it states about intimidation. Intimidation could be either without weapon (I'll kill your mother) or with weapon (bags or life). Could be weapon just a bonus dice maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wouldn't give the benefit of Hard Leverage if the actor can't back the threat up. &quot;I'll kill your mother if you don't do what I say&quot; isn't really leverage if your mother is safe in her home 10,000 miles away. It's still an attempt to coerce you into doing what they want, but it's not leveraged with anything. It's an empty threat. Now, if your mother is there and they've got a gun to her head or a knife to her throat, or if they show you a live feed of your mother bound and gagged in a closet somewhere, that's leverage. Even if they have no intention of actually killing her, or the footage is faked, or whatever, they have something other than words to push you towards doing what they say.<br /> <br /> Re: dice pool bonus for having a weapon, that's effectively what Hard Leverage is. Sure, it's worded as &quot;removing doors&quot; instead of &quot;adding bonus dice&quot;, but in a Forcing Doors attempt, the number of Doors only matters in the sense that it sets the dice penalty. Adding +2 to the actor's pool or decreasing the penalty by 2 have the same net effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}